# setup.ps1 verifies the skills against checksums.sha256 before installing them
# (CWE-494, Download of Code Without Integrity Check). Get-FileHash hashes the
# bytes on disk, so if a clone rewrites line endings the hashes shift and a
# perfectly legitimate download is rejected with "Integrity check FAILED".
#
# Measured 2026-08-24: with core.autocrlf=true the check passed 10/10, with
# core.autocrlf=false it failed 10/10. Both are ordinary settings - the first is
# the Git for Windows default, the second is what "checkout as-is" and every WSL
# or Linux clone gives you.
#
# eol=lf overrides core.autocrlf, so every clone gets identical bytes and the
# manifest is generated against the same content the installer will hash.
plugins/shift-left-security/skills/** text eol=lf

# setup.ps1 (2026-08-26) bundles setup/ alongside the skill and checksum-
# verifies it the same way, for the same CWE-494 reason - same fix needed here.
# Found by actually testing a sparse-clone install rather than by inspection:
# 3 of 13 files failed verification because the manifest had been generated
# against whatever line endings happened to already be on disk (a mix, per
# each file's own edit history), not against the git blob every clone gets.
setup/** text eol=lf
